control_assertion:
We have the equations \begin{align*} \tag{1}
\frac{a+b+c}{3}=6 \Rightarrow a+b+c&=18 \\ \tag{2}
c-4&=a\\ \tag{3}
b+4&=\frac{3}{5}(a+4)
\end{align*} From Equation (3), we have $b=\frac{3}{5}(a+4)-4$.

recovery_assertion:
We have the equations \begin{align*} \tag{1}
\frac{3}{a+b+c}=6 \Rightarrow a+b+c&=18 \\ \tag{2}
c-4&=a\\ \tag{3}
b+4&=\frac{3}{5}(a+4)
\end{align*} From Equation (3), we have $b=\frac{3}{5}(a+4)-4$.

control_assertion:
If $AB$ is a diameter, that means the triangle must have a right angle at $C.$ Therefore, we have that \begin{align*}
\angle B &= 180^\circ - (\angle A + \angle C) \\
&= 180^\circ - (14^\circ + 90^\circ) = \boxed{76^\circ}.
\end{align*}

recovery_assertion:
If $AB$ is a diameter, that means the triangle must have a right angle at $C.$ Therefore, we have that \begin{align*}
\angle B &= 180^\circ - (\angle A - \angle C) \\
&= 180^\circ - (14^\circ + 90^\circ) = \boxed{76^\circ}.
\end{align*}

